   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Describe",
   "texto": [
    "Behind «sein», the adjective **no cambia**: **Er ist groß** (he is high), **Sie ist groß** (she is high), **Sie sind groß** (are high).",
    "In front of a name it does carry completion; for now it learns these two as formulas: **lange Haare** (long hair) and **kurze Haare** (short hair).",
    "«Su»: **sein** (of it) and **ihr** (of it). They change like «ein»: **seine Frau** (his wife, of him), **ihr Mann** (her husband, of her)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "From 20 to 1,000",
   "texto": [
    "In German the units are said to be **antes** that the tens, together with **und**: 21 is **einundzwanzig** («one and twenty»), 35 is **fünfunddreißig**. It's all written together.",
    "The tens end up in **-zig**, except **dreißig** (30). One hundred is **hundert**, two hundred **zweihundert** and one thousand **tausend**. For 101 you can say **hunderteins**."
   ]
